<!doctype html>
<html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Deadbolt Stakeholder Report — {{ meta.run_id }}</title>
<style>
:root{--ink:#17212b;--muted:#687582;--line:#dfe5e9;--brand:#087e9b;--paper:#fff;--bg:#edf1f3;--critical:#a41025;--high:#c43c22;--medium:#9b6500;--low:#397026}*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;background:var(--bg);color:var(--ink);font:15px/1.55 Inter,system-ui,sans-serif}.page{max-width:960px;margin:28px auto;background:var(--paper);padding:48px 56px;box-shadow:0 2px 16px #17212b16}header{border-bottom:3px solid var(--brand);padding-bottom:24px}.eyebrow{color:var(--brand);font-size:11px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase}h1{font-size:29px;margin:5px 0}h2{font-size:19px;margin:34px 0 12px}.muted{color:var(--muted)}.summary{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.5fr 1fr;gap:22px;margin-top:24px}.panel{background:#f7f9fa;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:8px;padding:20px}.risk{font-size:34px;font-weight:800;text-transform:uppercase}.critical{color:var(--critical)}.high{color:var(--high)}.medium{color:var(--medium)}.low{color:var(--low)}.counts{display:flex;gap:9px;flex-wrap:wrap}.count{border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:6px;padding:10px 13px;min-width:90px}.count strong{font-size:21px;display:block}.finding{border-top:1px solid var(--line);padding:17px 0}.tag{font-size:10px;font-weight:800;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.06em}.scope{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:10px}.metric{padding:14px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:6px}.metric strong{font-size:22px;display:block}.notice{border-left:4px solid #d09a27;background:#fff8e8;padding:13px 16px}.appendix{margin-top:48px;border-top:3px solid var(--brand);padding-top:24px}.inventory{columns:2;column-gap:26px;padding-left:22px}.inventory li{break-inside:avoid;margin:3px 0;font-size:12px;overflow-wrap:anywhere}footer{border-top:1px solid var(--line);margin-top:40px;padding-top:16px;color:var(--muted);font-size:12px}@media(max-width:700px){.page{margin:0;padding:28px}.summary{grid-template-columns:1fr}.scope{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}.inventory{columns:1}}@media print{body{background:white}.page{box-shadow:none;margin:0;max-width:none}.appendix{break-before:page}.inventory-section{break-inside:avoid}}
</style></head><body><main class="page">
<header><div class="eyebrow">Deadbolt / Stakeholder brief</div><h1>{{ domain|upper }} Security Assessment</h1><div class="muted">{{ assessment_profile }} profile · {{ meta.run_id }} · {{ meta.finished_at[:10] }} · Deadbolt {{ meta.deadbolt_version }}</div></header>

<section class="summary"><div class="panel"><div class="muted">Highest automated risk signal</div><div class="risk {{ highest_severity }}">{{ highest_severity }}</div><p>{% if findings %}The assessment produced {{ findings|length }} reportable security signal{{ '' if findings|length == 1 else 's' }}. These require analyst validation before being treated as confirmed vulnerabilities.{% else %}No automated security signals met the {{ min_severity|upper }} reporting threshold. This does not establish that the target is free of vulnerabilities.{% endif %}</p></div><div class="panel"><div class="muted">Signals by severity</div><div class="counts">{% for severity in ['critical','high','medium','low'] %}<div class="count"><strong class="{{ severity }}">{{ severity_counts.get(severity,0) }}</strong><span>{{ severity|title }}</span></div>{% endfor %}</div></div></section>

<h2>Executive summary</h2><p>Deadbolt performed an automated {{ domain }} assessment across the authorized scope. It discovered and validated reachable attack surface, then tested eligible assets for known vulnerability patterns. Results below are prioritized for review and remediation planning.</p><p class="muted">Authorization boundary: <strong>{{ scope_snapshot }}</strong>{% if scope_hash != 'Not recorded' %} · SHA-256 {{ scope_hash[:12] }}…{% endif %}</p>

<h2>Priority observations</h2>{% for f in findings %}<div class="finding"><div class="tag {{ f.severity }}">{{ f.severity }} · {{ f.verification_status }}</div><strong>{{ f.title }}</strong><p>{{ f.metadata.description or ('Automated detection on ' ~ f.asset ~ '. Technical validation is required.') }}</p></div>{% else %}<p>No priority observations met the reporting threshold.</p>{% endfor %}

<h2>Assessment reach</h2><div class="scope">{% for stage in coverage %}<div class="metric"><strong>{{ stage.value }}</strong><span class="muted">{{ stage.label }}</span></div>{% endfor %}</div>

<h2>Limitations and assurance</h2><div class="notice"><ul>{% for item in limitations %}<li>{{ item }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul></div><p>This report summarizes automated coverage. Authentication, authorization, business logic and other context-dependent risks require analyst-led testing and are not implied to be covered unless explicitly documented.</p>

<h2>Recommended next actions</h2><ol><li>Validate each automated security signal and record confirmed or false-positive status.</li><li>Review assets excluded by authorization scope and expand scope only with written approval.</li><li>Perform targeted manual testing of authentication, authorization, sensitive workflows and business logic.</li><li>Retest confirmed findings after remediation and preserve evidence in the assessment run.</li></ol>
<footer>Concise stakeholder report. URL inventories, tool execution, exclusions, and evidence are available in <strong>technical-report.html</strong>.</footer>
</main></body></html>
